diff --git a/src/channels/docs/adapters.md b/src/channels/docs/adapters.md
index 41f6665..5b598b5 100644
--- a/src/channels/docs/adapters.md
+++ b/src/channels/docs/adapters.md
@@ -31,3 +31,72 @@ Microsoft Teams ([msteams-channel](../msteams/msteams-channel.ts), ATO-506) uses
 Shared model commands currently import provider persistence from TUI; stage 02 moves that responsibility. Do not describe this boundary as already repaired.
 
 Sources: [Telegram](../telegram/telegram-channel.ts), [Discord](../discord/discord-channel.ts), [Swarm](../swarm/swarm-registry.ts), [model commands](../model-command.ts), [backoff](../reconnect-backoff.ts). Tests: [Telegram](../telegram/telegram-channel.test.ts), [cron](../telegram/cron-command.test.ts), [Discord](../discord/discord-channel.test.ts), [model commands](../telegram/inbound-model-command.test.ts).
+
+## Desktop session continuation
+
+TUI turns mark their session with `metadata.desktopTelegramBridge` inside the FIFO
+callback, after reloading saved state. The legacy `macTelegramBridge` marker is
+accepted when reading existing sessions. The bridge uses platform-neutral runtime APIs. The paired owner's
+private Telegram DM may connect through `/desktop [session-id]`. With no ID it picks the only running marked session, or the most recent
+marked session when all are idle. Multiple running sessions require an explicit
+ID. Incognito sessions and other channels are excluded.
+
+`/status` and `/result` read the selected session without inference. English
+natural-language equivalents include “How far along are you?” and “Show me the
+result of your analysis”. Legacy German input phrases remain accepted. Control
+messages are English, and follow-up turns request English replies. Stored answers
+and plan text are returned verbatim, preserving the original analysis.
+
+Other messages and `/queue <request>` use the same session's FIFO `runtime.runTurn`,
+waiting for current work and reloading saved context at the queue boundary.
+Up to 20 requests may be outstanding per chat, including attachments.
+Session eligibility is rechecked before each queued request starts. A serial queue tracks their abort
+signals and size while status/result messages bypass execution. Approvals bind on the remote turn's first event and
+release on its terminal event and in cleanup. Status reads and queued requests
+do not move a desktop turn's approval route. A stored active turn that this
+runtime does not own must be resumed in this terminal before a remote follow-up.
+
+`/desktop off` or `/new` returns the private chat to its own Telegram conversation.
+The terminal process must stay running; this feature does not connect separate
+Atomic processes or start a desktop session on another computer.
+
+`/cancel` cancels outstanding Telegram requests. `/stop` also calls the runtime
+turn controller's cancellation hook for the currently owning desktop turn.
+Hooks are installed only while a submission owns its session and removed at
+settlement. The runtime combines its cancellation signal with the caller's
+signal. Tool cancellation remains cooperative, preserving completed effects.
+Channel shutdown cancels all remote queues before stopping its active turns.
+
+## Telegram desktop plan review
+
+The desktop bridge's `/review` command ([review](../telegram/desktop-review.ts),
+[Git snapshot](../telegram/desktop-review-git.ts)) shows the latest final answer
+as a proposed plan, a summary of all staged/unstaged/untracked changes in that
+repository, and retained shell verification evidence from the latest request.
+`/review diff` also includes the tracked-file patch. It performs no inference,
+executes no tests, and changes neither files nor the Git index. Tool status is
+not presented as proof that a test suite passed; missing/truncated evidence is
+explicit. The report masks recognized credentials and known environment secrets.
+
+Only an idle linked desktop session with no outstanding Telegram work can be
+reviewed. The whole report must be delivered before a separate message offers
+**Approve plan** / **Reject plan**. Reject only dismisses the review; it does not
+revert existing changes. Approval queues implementation of the exact answer
+that was shown, with ordinary tool permissions still enforced. This is a plan
+workflow, not a global requirement for every other chat command or local edit.
+
+Review buttons are random one-use tokens bound to the paired owner, private
+chat, keyboard message and selected session. They expire after 30 minutes;
+a new review, reconnect or shutdown invalidates old buttons. Session history
+and plan state plus Git HEAD, index diff and working-tree bytes are checked
+again on approval and under the runtime FIFO before inference. The runtime's
+local `beforeRun` precondition is not available in goal mode. Queued approvals
+cannot silently apply to changed sessions. External programs do not share this
+lock: a review is a freshness check, not a filesystem transaction or rollback.
+
+Snapshots are bounded to 10,000 tracked/untracked files, 64 MiB of file bytes,
+2 MiB per Git command and 10 seconds per Git command. Ignored untracked files
+are outside the snapshot. Symlinks/submodules and incomplete snapshots are
+refused; a report above 32,000 characters cannot produce an approval. Large
+projects must narrow their worktree or be reviewed locally. The snapshot hashes
+untracked content but does not display it in the patch.
